Fillets: two stripes of one radius R at a vertex, one running on into the
ball of an earlier rounding of R (the ball staying put there), the other
ending on two planes that ball touches, meet at that ball's section
(mitcad#1427).

A wall W of an opening through a plate meets the plate's top T and a side
P (along a crease of a few degrees); T's edge with P was rounded with R
earlier (a cylinder K), and that rounding goes on into a torus of R along
an arc. A later feature's face X (an extrusion of the torus's section,
tangent to T) lies between T and the torus at W. The opening's edges on W
are rounded with R. W's boundary turns at the vertex V where its edge
with X meets its edge with the torus (X and the torus meet at a crease):
two contours. A rounds W's edges with T and X, B those with the torus, K
and P. The ball of B over the torus and K stays put (both tubes of R whose
centre lines run through its centre C, which lies R from W, T and P); A's
ball rolls on W and T (its contact passes over X onto T) up to a section
short of C. The stored body after the rounding has A's cylinder run
straight on to C's section, B's ball over K from P's rounding up to that
section (a sphere's corner patch), and X and the torus's part at V gone
under the ball. OCCT's corner at V (PerformTwoCorner) failed ("BRep_Tool::
no parameters on surface").

- JoinAtStillBalls (new, in ChFi3d_Builder_StillBall.cxx, after
  JoinAcrossCorners): for a vertex of two stripes of one constant radius
  R, A's end pieces on two planes W and T up to a cylinder of R whose
  contacts are unbounded lines, and a section of B at the end of one of
  its pieces towards V whose contacts lie on those lines at one section of
  the cylinder (centre C on its axis, R from both contacts): A's
  run-on to there within 8 R beyond its end, its contacts on W's and T's
  faces, and B past there over edges between W and tubes of R about a
  curve through C (a cylinder of R whose axis runs through C, or a torus
  of minor radius R whose centre circle does). Then the cylinder piece is
  run on to that section (its points B's), A's pieces past it and B's past
  that section are dropped, and the two ends meet there as free ends: the
  points and the section's edge shared, as JoinOverNarrowFaceFrom's ends
  meet. The vertices' corners are those of the ends left.

On the reported design's body before the item (OCCT alone), the wall's
whole loop with radius 0.2: valid, every new face within 8e-6 mm of the
stored body after the item and its faces within 7e-6 mm of the result;
the change of volume -0.053063 against the file's -0.052871 mm3, the
difference the input's own outside the item (faces of other features
1e-4 to 2.7e-4 mm off the stored body). Through MitCad's import the item
is parametric and verified, the final body the file's within 2e-8 of its
volume. Needs 1600 (the corner balls of the same chain at the other
corner of the wall). Before, the corners at both vertices failed.

